          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Briscola a 31 where the first player or side to reach 31 points (from card points in tricks) wins the round.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Trump is the suit of the turned card; follow suit when able. Card points (ace 11, three 10, king 4, queen 3, jack 2) are summed from tricks; first to 31 wins.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit; point values: ace 11, three 10, king 4, queen 3, jack 2, others zero. Trick order is standard Briscola. The round ends when a player or partnership reaches 31 points from captured cards.',
